# Godot's import cache and generated metadata.
game/.godot/
game/android/build/
*.translation

# Build output.
build/

# The pinned engines. Fetched by tools\setup\install-godot.ps1, not committed -
# they are ~180 MB each and everyone gets the identical file from the same URL.
tools/godot/
tools/godot-mono/

# ai-game.dev (godot_mcp): the local MCP server binary (~99 MB), its logs, and
# the signed-in credential. The addon itself IS committed, under
# game/addons/godot_mcp, so everyone runs the same version.
game/.ai-game-dev/
game/.godot-mcp/

# .NET build intermediates. Godot.NET.Sdk puts most of them under game/.godot/
# already, but not all of them.
game/obj/
game/bin/
game/*.sln

# The art applications, ~880 MB together. Fetched by
# tools\art\install-art-tools.ps1.
tools/art/pixelorama/
tools/art/material-maker/
tools/art/krita/

# Source art packs: commit only the ones the build actually reads, so the game's
# art is reproducible offline without carrying thousands of unused files. The
# rest are one command away: python.exe tools\art\fetch_assets.py
art-source/kenney/*
!art-source/kenney/roguelike-indoors/

# LPC character art, ~400 MB. Too big to commit; fetched on demand with
# python.exe tools\art\fetch_assets.py --lpc
art-source/lpc/

# Never. Signing keys live in C:\temp\_secrets.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
steam_appid.txt
**/secrets.*

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Journey backdrops WERE excluded here: the originals came from an image
# generator with a visible watermark and unsettled licensing, and a missing
# backdrop in a fresh clone was the signal that it still needed replacing.
#
# That reason expired on 2026-09-22. All 69 were regenerated through kling
# (C:\temp\aitools), unwatermarked, same provenance as the journey2 set that
# is already tracked. journey.json names every backdrop by scene id, so a
# clone without them cannot run - which is why they are tracked now.
# Offline placeholders, if ever needed: tools/art/build_journey_scenes.py --replace

# My own byproducts, not part of the game.
# backup/ is the timestamped copies taken before editing data files.
# preview/ is screenshots captured from built exes for eyeballing.
backup/
preview/
# art-source/working/ was excluded here as "scratch output from the tile-index
# helpers". It is kept now, on instruction: 35 images, 876 KB, and it is art.

# Timestamped snapshots taken before regenerating a batch of art - backdrops,
# iran, palestine, runs, sheets. They are copies of what is already in
# game/assets/art, ~355 MB of them, and nothing reads them.
backup/

# Generated previews: screenshots of every screen plus the text dumps
# (all_text.csv / .html). Produced on demand by the preview tooling, ~21 MB.
preview/

# Large files that are neither source nor needed to run: keep video and archive
# formats out, they belong in C:\temp\_assets or C:\temp\_graphics.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
